Part of #90684

## What Problem This Solves

Synology Chat users receive bot replies containing internal assistant tool-trace scaffolding lines (e.g. `⚠️ 🛠️ \`search repos (agent)\` failed`) leaked into outbound chat messages. These banners are internal runtime diagnostics that should not reach end users.

Synology Chat's outbound adapter defines `deliveryMode`, `textChunkLimit`, `sendText`, and `sendMedia` — but no `sanitizeText` hook. Raw assistant text goes straight to `sendSynologyChatText` without sanitization.

## Why This Change Was Made

This adds `sanitizeAssistantVisibleText` as the `sanitizeText` hook on Synology Chat's outbound adapter. This matches the accepted sibling pattern already shipped for Slack, Signal, Matrix, Feishu, Mattermost, Telegram, Google Chat, QQBot, IRC, SMS, Discord, WhatsApp, and LINE.

The fix is narrowly scoped: one import + one hook on the existing outbound block. No new abstraction, no config changes, no behavioral change for normal prose.

## User Impact

Synology Chat users no longer see internal tool-trace failure banners in bot replies. Normal assistant prose passes through unchanged.

## Evidence

### Negative control — core stripInternalRuntimeScaffolding keeps banner (pre-fix behavior)

```
$ node --import tsx -e '
import { stripInternalRuntimeScaffolding } from "./src/infra/outbound/sanitize-text.js";
const text = "Done.\n⚠️ 🛠️ \`search repos (agent)\` failed";
const result = stripInternalRuntimeScaffolding(text);
console.log("=== Negative control: core stripInternalRuntimeScaffolding ===");
console.log("Input:", JSON.stringify(text));
console.log("Output:", JSON.stringify(result));
console.log("Banner survives (core strip does NOT catch tool-trace):", result.includes("⚠️"));
'
=== Negative control: core stripInternalRuntimeScaffolding ===
Input: "Done.\n⚠️ 🛠️ `search repos (agent)` failed"
Output: "Done.\n⚠️ 🛠️ `search repos (agent)` failed"
Banner survives (core strip does NOT catch tool-trace): true
```

### After fix — synologyChatPlugin.outbound.sanitizeText strips banner

```
$ node --import tsx -e '
import { synologyChatPlugin } from "./extensions/synology-chat/src/channel.js";

// Test 1: prose + tool-trace banner stripped
const text = "Done.\n⚠️ 🛠️ \`search repos (agent)\` failed";
const result = synologyChatPlugin.outbound?.sanitizeText?.({ text, payload: { text } });
console.log("=== After fix: synologyChatPlugin.outbound.sanitizeText ===");
console.log("Test 1 — prose + banner:");
console.log("  Input:", JSON.stringify(text));
console.log("  Output:", JSON.stringify(result));
console.log("  Banner stripped:", !result?.includes("⚠️"));
console.log("  Prose preserved:", result?.includes("Done."));

// Test 2: normal prose unchanged
const prose = "The pipeline has 3 open deals.";
const proseResult = synologyChatPlugin.outbound?.sanitizeText?.({ text: prose, payload: { text: prose } });
console.log("Test 2 — normal prose:");
console.log("  Input:", JSON.stringify(prose));
console.log("  Output:", JSON.stringify(proseResult));
console.log("  Prose unchanged:", proseResult === prose);

// Test 3: trace-only is dropped
const traceOnly = "⚠️ 🛠️ \`search repos (agent)\` failed";
const traceResult = synologyChatPlugin.outbound?.sanitizeText?.({ text: traceOnly, payload: { text: traceOnly } });
console.log("Test 3 — trace-only:");
console.log("  Input:", JSON.stringify(traceOnly));
console.log("  Output:", JSON.stringify(traceResult));
console.log("  Trace-only empty:", traceResult?.trim() === "" || traceResult === "");
console.log("\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS PASSED");
'
=== After fix: synologyChatPlugin.outbound.sanitizeText ===
Test 1 — prose + banner:
  Input: "Done.\n⚠️ 🛠️ `search repos (agent)` failed"
  Output: "Done."
  Banner stripped: true
  Prose preserved: true
Test 2 — normal prose:
  Input: "The pipeline has 3 open deals."
  Output: "The pipeline has 3 open deals."
  Prose unchanged: true
Test 3 — trace-only:
  Input: "⚠️ 🛠️ `search repos (agent)` failed"
  Output: ""
  Trace-only empty: true

ALL PROOF ASSERTIONS PASSED
```

### Vitest regression tests

```
$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/synology-chat/src/channel.test.ts --run
 Test Files  1 passed (1)
      Tests  40 passed (40)

$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/synology-chat/src/approval-auth.test.ts extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts extensions/synology-chat/src/core.test.ts --run
 Test Files  3 passed (3)
      Tests  47 passed (47)
```

### What was not tested

- Did not test against a live Synology Chat NAS instance (requires Synology hardware/credentials). The sanitizer is tested at the function-call boundary — the same `sanitizeAssistantVisibleText` helper is already proven in production across 12+ channels.
- Proof is at the exported plugin hook layer (`synologyChatPlugin.outbound.sanitizeText`), not a unit mock — this is the real function that the outbound delivery pipeline calls at runtime.
